<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Microsoft reports it is =E2=80=9Cseeing po=
sitive results=E2=80=9D in its efforts to get its services back online for =
millions of customers around the world.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Users, organisations and businesses have b=
een affected by problems with some of the tech company=E2=80=99s systems, i=
ncluding Microsoft 365, Teams and Outlook.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">However, it said: =E2=80=9CWe=E2=80=99re s=
eeing positive results for server stability after applying an upstream auth=
entication/routing configuration component patch to a portion of our infras=
tructure. We=E2=80=99ll continue to monitor its progress and are working to=
 expand it to servers supporting active regions coming online.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Microsoft does not think the disruption is=
 because of a cyber-attack. It said: =E2=80=9CAs of now, we are not aware o=
f any malicious activity that is causing this incident. We will continue to=
 treat this incident with urgency and priority until full resolution. Once =
mitigated, we will provide full details of the root cause, defense-in-depth=
 repair items, and more within a post-incident report.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">British government engineers are working w=
ith Microsoft to assess the impact of the outage, according to a UK ministe=
r.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">However, he could not confirm whether any =
government systems had been affected.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Several UK police forces have urged people=
 not to report crimes online because of the Microsoft outage. People have b=
een told to telephone them instead.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The outage has caused disruption among com=
panies and government ministries in Japan, forcing staff to turn to analogu=
e methods to distribute information and contact clients.</p>
